# Example ~/.arrangrr.init — copy to $HOME/.arrangrr.init to use it.
#
# The live TUI auto-runs ~/.arrangrr.init on every launch (no flag), after the
# panels open and ~/.arrangrr.rc is applied. It is a plain list of shell
# commands (the same grammar the REPL accepts). It is LENIENT: a bad line only
# warns to the console and startup continues — a stale default never bricks the
# TUI. An explicit `--init FILE` overrides the auto-load and is STRICT (a bad
# line aborts). Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# This example configures the "single-finger live steering" session: you play
# one key on the CHORDS panel and that key alone imposes the chord the whole
# band follows.
#
# TWO PLAYABLE SURFACES (selected by which panel is focused — no pitch split):
#   - the PIANO panel is the MELODY surface: its keys SOUND and steer nobody.
#   - the CHORDS panel is the HARMONY surface: the SAME keys are SILENT there
#     but re-harmonize the band (they feed the chord detector). Focus it (TAB or
#     its panel number) and play to steer. Detection is ON out of the box, so no
#     `chord detect on` is needed here anymore — the chords panel already steers.

# Single-finger chords: one held key = the scale-aware maj/min triad (a second
# key colours it). This applies to the harmony surface (the chords panel).
chord mode single

# Only your live keys (played on the chords panel) steer the band. The chord
# sequencer and `chord play` never override your finger (DESIGN.md D47).
chord follow detect

# Load a style so there is a band to hear. Swap for any builtin:
#   basic pop rock ballad funk disco house swing bossa samba
#   reggae country blues shuffle latin motown
style load basic

# The band is NOT started automatically — press CTRL+P to play/stop.
# To auto-start it on launch instead, uncomment the next line:
# transport start
